  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (scgpt, resnet50, avgpool, weighted, multiprofile) achieves 0.525 acc, while image-only (config_005) is only 0.208, confirming both modalities contribute. The single most impactful untested dimension is the image backbone: upgrading resnet50 (~25M params) to imagenet_vit_l (~300M params) is the largest representational capacity jump available. This experiment (config_018) changes only the image encoder from resnet50 to imagenet_vit_l while holding all other settings identical to the current best (scgpt, multiprofile, avgpool, weighted), isolating the effect of a stronger visual backbone. If it improves accuracy meaningfully, subsequent experiments can exploit ViT-L with transformer aggregation or different fusion; if it does not, we redirect to RNA-encoder or aggregation changes. Expected relative cost: roughly 2–3× config_002 (~8–12 GPU hours) due to ViT-L's larger parameter count and higher per-step compute, but this is justified as it is the most likely single change to yield the largest accuracy gain within our remaining 7-experiment budget."
}

